id: metamoran-style
name: Metamoran Style
# The Metamorese Fusion's Method Trait: given as a Fusion is fused by that Method (fusion-make.mjs), never picked by hand.
fusionMethod: metamorese
description: >
  The unique fashion of the Metamoran people materializes on your newly-formed body, giving you great power in addition to style points.
text: >
  Metamoran Style: The unique fashion of the Metamoran people materializes on your newly-formed body, giving you great power in addition to style points.
  (1)-[Automatic/Start of Combat Encounter]: Instead of gaining the Apparel of the Fused Characters, this Fusion gains and equips the Metamoran Clothing (shown below).
  (2)-[Passive]: Increase your Stress Bonus by 2.
  (3)-[Passive]: While you are in a Transformation with a Tier of Power Requirement of 4+, you may apply the Divine Apparel Special Apparel Quality to the Metamoran Clothing Apparel.
  (4)-[Triggered/Start of Turn, 1/Encounter]: You may use a Maneuver with an Action Cost of 1 Action as an Out-of-Sequence Maneuver.
  (5)-[Triggered/Start of Combat Encounter]: Gain 2 Karma Points. You lose these Karma Points if they are not spent before the Fusion splits back into its Fused Characters.

---

[passive]
# (1) and (3): the Metamoran Clothing, made and worn as the Fusion is fused - in place of the Fused Characters' Apparel
# (fusion-make.mjs).
# (2)
stressBonus += 2;

# (4) On your turn's card, ticked - never Automatic, it hands over an Out-of-Sequence Maneuver: a Maneuver of yours of 1 Action
# (fusion-traits.mjs oneActionOutOfSequence).
[triggered/start-of-turn, 1/encounter, outOfSequence, effect 4]
oneActionOutOfSequence();

# (5) Entering the Encounter: 2 Karma Points. Losing them as the Fusion splits is the table's - splitting is (the user's).
# Automatic by default, its Triggered/Automatic button.
[triggered/start-of-encounter, effect 5]
gainKarma(2);
